a quick video about what is it I  actually do so I work within a  recruitment industry and I work as a  recruitment consultant now what the hell  does a recruitment consultant actually  do now let me tell you it's loads  absolutely loads there's a common  misperception out there that recruiters  will loads of cash quick they'll always  be taken at their clients for fancy  dinners they're always attending  networking events drinking loads of  alcohol now we do do some of that but  there's so much that goes behind the  scenes that recruiters don't always  share or whatever and I think that's why  it's important that I wanted to share  this on this video so look the nuts and  bolts of it is business owners will pay  us recruitment consultants to find them  the right people that's how we earn our  money okay now what goes into finding  the right people is the toughest part  now a lot of people also with the  misperception is that we probably simply  as recruiters post a job advert on  LinkedIn a job advert on online job  boards and let the candidates come to us  now this couldn't be further from the  truth I've been in recruitment now for  going towards two and a half years and  I've never placed a candidate who's  applied for my job directly it just it  just doesn't happen in my opinion anyway  so we have to be proactive with the  tools that we have at our fingertips so  it's our database it's our own  individual networks it's using the  online job boards and some of the  Seavey's that we can find using LinkedIn  and the best recruiters will maximize  all of those tools the best it really is  how you use them so the first thing is  that that's what's gone on behind the  scenes we spend hours each day trying to  find the right people leaving voicemails  sending emails text messages spending  the late nights in the office all to  speak to the right people now what do we  also do we manage  was expectations that would be the  business owners and what they're looking  to pay what they can get in the market  and also candidates what can they  achieve what's realistic what isn't so  with that as well is we help throughout  the process so it's not a similar to  funding like people get over this it's  all done and dusted it's coaching the  client throughout in terms of what are  the motivation for the cabinet's there  that they're speaking to make sure  they're getting those things sort of  across candidates preparing them for the  interview go through that with them what  they shouldn't say what they should say  and then also a huge part of it when it  gets to the latter end of the stages is  basically making sure that both parties  are happy and that's the candidate and  the client the Kanaks happen with what's  on offer and the clients happy with what  they're offering suit to the candidate  is worth it's in their budget so you  have to manage expectations throughout  that process and then also you have to  negotiate you have to negotiate and the  client's behalf they have to negotiate  on the candidates behalf again to make  sure that both parties are happy now  there's so much that goes into being a  recruitment consultant and that's what  makes it so addictive and so fulfilling  when you have a client or a candidate  who calls you or send your mission goes  you know what you've done amazing there  you've happen to get an amazing job or  you've happen to get the perfect person  that's what it's all about so what  recruitment consultants don't do is put  their feet up and let the candidates  come to us trip loads of beer and loads  of money in the first six months no  there's so much hard work that goes into  it and that's why it's one of the best  jobs out there nothing more people  should be considering working in  recruitment  [Music]
 

